If we can see the above still we are seeing the prod name space has only one pod running.
The sidecar pod is still missing.

To resolve this issue we need to label our name space
root@master-node:/home/master# kubectl get ns --show-labels
NAME               STATUS   AGE    LABELS
calico-apiserver   Active   14d    kubernetes.io/metadata.name=calico-apiserver,name=calico-apiserver,pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce-version=latest,pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce=privileged
calico-system      Active   14d    kubernetes.io/metadata.name=calico-system,name=calico-system,pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce-version=latest,pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce=privileged
default            Active   14d    kubernetes.io/metadata.name=default
istio-system       Active   113m   istio-injection=disabled,kubernetes.io/metadata.name=istio-system
kube-node-lease    Active   14d    kubernetes.io/metadata.name=kube-node-lease
kube-public        Active   14d    kubernetes.io/metadata.name=kube-public
kube-system        Active   14d    kubernetes.io/metadata.name=kube-system
metallb-system     Active   14d    kubernetes.io/metadata.name=metallb-system,pod-security.kubernetes.io/audit=privileged,pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce=privileged,pod-security.kubernetes.io/warn=privileged
prod               Active   95m    kubernetes.io/metadata.name=prod
tigera-operator    Active   14d    kubernetes.io/metadata.name=tigera-operator,name=tigera-operator

Look @ istio-system namespace
istio-system       Active   113m   istio-injection=disabled,kubernetes.io/metadata.name=istio-system

To enable label the prod name space use below

root@master-node:/home/master# kubectl label ns prod istio-injection=enabled --overwrite
namespace/prod labeled


prod               Active   102m   istio-injection=enable,kubernetes.io/metadata.name=prod

Once istio-injection label is enabled
You need to do the deployment restart for istio pod running

Before
root@master-node:/home/master# kubectl get pod -n prod
NAME                       READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE
node-app-f76bb96b8-95ggj   1/1     Running   0          97m
root@master-node:/home/master#

root@master-node:/home/master# kubectl get deployment -n prod
NAME       READY   UP-TO-DATE   AVAILABLE   AGE
node-app   1/1     1            1           98m

After
kubectl -n prod rollout restart deploy node-app

if istio is enabled for prod namespace you will be sidecard pod along with your application pod

